  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 124 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery continues to show a weak mid/upper trough \ndrifting slowly eastward across the Southern Plains while more \nrobust WSW mid/upper flow prevailed across the Northern Plains. A \nclipper system was also evident over the Northern Plains which was \nmoving southeast towards the Upper Mississippi Valley area. This \nclipper system will drive a weak frontal boundary southward across \nthe area late tonight into early Wed. This will allow winds to shift \nto the northwest while ushering in drier air. Ahead of this frontal \nboundary across parts of southern and southeast KS we could see some \nfog redevelop during the predawn hours on Wed when winds decouple \nand low level moisture isn't scoured ahead of the front.\n\nBreezy northwest winds are anticipated in the wake of the front on \nWed and with much drier air expected to advect across the area. This \nwill result in above average temperatures with most areas seeing \nhighs in the upper 60s/around 70.\n\nAnother shortwave trough is progged to pivot around the Great Lakes \nlow driving a reinforcing shot of cooler air across the area on Thu. \nHighs may occur early in the period with a sharp E-W gradient across \nthe forecast area. Early highs may climb into the lower 60s before \nfalling later in the day. Trended minimum temperatures lower in \neastern KS Thu night/Fri morning as high pressure noses into the \narea.\n\nTemperatures will begin to moderate from west to east on Fri as \nsoutherly low level flow returns. This could result in a sharper \nthermal gradient across the forecast area with seasonably cool \nvalues expected. Most areas are expected to see highs in the 50s.\n\nA mid/upper ridge is progged to build across the central CONUS late \nin the week and into the beginning of the weekend before another \nshortwave trough emerges from the Rockies late in the weekend. This \nsystem will bring increasing chances for showers to the area Sat \nnight-Sun night. Seasonably mild temperatures will follow for early \nnext week as mid/upper ridging returns to the central CONUS.",
